## 3. API Proto Message (protobuf)

There are two proto files relevant to Memo:

### 3a. API-level Memo message
**File:** `/bench/home/work/proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto` -- line 198

```protobuf
message Memo {
  string name = 1;                           // Resource name: memos/{memo}
  State state = 2;
  string creator = 3;                        // Format: users/{user}
  google.protobuf.Timestamp create_time = 4;
  google.protobuf.Timestamp update_time = 5;
  // field 6 reserved (was display_time)
  string content = 7;                        // Markdown format
  Visibility visibility = 9;
  repeated string tags = 10;                 // Extracted from content
  bool pinned = 11;
  repeated Attachment attachments = 12;
  repeated MemoRelation relations = 13;
  repeated Reaction reactions = 14;
  Property property = 15;                    // Computed properties
  optional string parent = 16;              // Parent memo name
  string snippet = 17;                      // Plain text snippet
  optional Location location = 18;

  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    string title = 5;
  }
}
```

### 3b. Store-level MemoPayload message
**File:** `/bench/home/work/proto/store/memo.proto` -- line 7

```protobuf
message MemoPayload {
  Property property = 1;
  Location location = 2;
  repeated string tags = 3;

  message Property { ... }
  message Location { ... }
}
```

This is the internal storage payload serialized into the `payload` column in the SQL table.

